An acceptance criterion (facet) is a verifiable condition attached to exactly one requirement version — not a separate requirement line and not a capability line. Facets shall have no independent trace graph; satisfaction is recorded on the parent requirement. Each facet shall use a testable 'shall' statement. A child requirement line (decomposition) is a distinct concept per ARCH-HIER-REQ-DECOMP.
