[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-KEY-JWKS
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Token signing keys: kid, JWKS, rotation with overlap window
STATEMENT: >>>
Each token signing key has a kid. By default it is a non-exportable OpenBao Transit key, so signing happens inside the KeyProvider and the kid is the key name plus version. The AS publishes public keys at its jwks_uri for the active key and any retired keys still inside the overlap window. Rotation is scheduled and on demand: a new key version starts signing, the prior version stays verify-only until the overlap window passes (at least the maximum access-token lifetime plus clock skew), and is then removed. After that, tokens with the retired kid are rejected.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: ARCH-KEY-JWKS
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: key:signing:rotate
priority: 5
iteration: iter-r1
security.catalog_ref: SC-12.3
security.verification_note: SC-12(3) asymmetric keys; SC-13; ASD V-222570.
edge: ← uses from ARCH-AUTH-AS
edge: ← uses from FIX-JWKS-ROTATION-OVERLAP
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-KEY-ENVELOPE
delivered_by_release: R1 — foundation shell + internal auth
edge: → conforms_to to SC-12.3 (pin imprint=nist-800-53@rev5-dogfood-20261006)
edge: → conforms_to to SC-13 (pin imprint=nist-800-53@rev5-dogfood-20261006)
edge: → conforms_to to V-222570 (pin imprint=asd-stig@v6r4)
