[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-KEY-FIPS
STATUS: Active
TITLE: FIPS-validated cryptographic modules where applicable
STATEMENT: >>>
Where a deployment requires it (DoD/federal profile), all cryptographic operations (hashing, signing, encryption, key wrap, and RNG for session IDs and tokens) use FIPS 140-validated modules (FIPS mode). Password hashing then uses PBKDF2 (ARCH-CRED-HASH), and a KeyProvider build that is not FIPS-validated is refused in that mode. Whether FIPS mode is the default for commercial deployments is an open question.
