STATEMENT: >>>
FIXTURE / TEST BED (not a product feature). MCP host (as alex-author) calls the MCP server without a token → 401 + WWW-Authenticate resource_metadata. It fetches PRM, then AS metadata (issuer match, S256 advertised), authorizes with S256 + resource=MCP URI, and exchanges code + verifier + resource for an aud=MCP access token plus a rotating refresh token. The tool update_draft then succeeds (200) after the audience check and RBAC.
