[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-DEVENV-IDENTITY.1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Seeded dev accounts on the internal AS; none in production
STATEMENT: >>>
Local development signs in through ReqAML's internal OAuth AS (ARCH-AUTH-AS) with seeded dev local accounts mapped to the dogfood seed identities, so A01/A02 sessions, grants, Scoped View, and MCP authorization can be exercised offline. Dev account credentials are never committed: they come from the local env file or are generated at first seed and shown locally. Seeded dev accounts and the dev seed loader are dev-only. Production builds and configs ship no seeded dev accounts and no default credentials, and the seed loader refuses to create accounts in production mode. In production, enterprise SSO federates through the same AS (ARCH-AUTH-FEDERATION). This replaces the earlier third-party local OIDC stub idea.
