[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CAP-RENAME-REQALM
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Product name correction: ReqALM (ALM, not AML)
STATEMENT: >>>
Repository, runtime identifiers, OAuth client IDs, env vars, and dogfood seed use the product name ReqALM (requirements + application lifecycle management). Persisted identifiers keep the legacy ReqAML spelling where renaming would orphan existing data: Compose volume names (reqaml-pg, reqaml-openbao, reqaml-secrets), OpenBao Transit key names (reqaml-kek, reqaml-dek-*) and an existing Postgres role/database. Existing dev stacks upgrade in place: migration 005 renames OAuth client ids, the project id and seeded grant ids, and `pnpm devenv:init` migrates .reqaml/ and REQAML_* names keeping secret values. Active requirement statements keep historical ReqAML prose until a content successor.
<<<
